+# Native stage admission repair
+
+User explicitly requested continuation and debugging. Implements the already approved C/D loop and native-scoring-stages.md policy; no new approval gate.
+
+## Constraints and architecture
+
+One scientific program retains its full comparison, data/code identity and pending scoring duties. Separate reviewed stages may prepare, check software, calibrate, train or export without fabricating a scored comparison. Only the adopted Work Harness C/D profile opts into this route. Online scoring dependencies cannot be deferred. Final scorer verification, B05/M05 and E remain unchanged. Each actual native execution has controller-owned identity and a runtime-generated per-attempt context. Prior results, jobs, usage and sources remain immutable.
+
+## Work
+
+- [x] Reproduce scorer-before-preparation rejection in isolated hn01 tests.
+- [x] Add strict native_stages.py contract validation and runtime context; connect runner/CD admission/NativeBridge, scoped legacy preservation.
+- [x] Test actual execution, tampering, predecessor lineage, scorer/gate separation and later score provenance on hn01.
+- [ ] Independent whole-change review, docs, version and manifest refresh; install and audited source adoption at quiet boundary.
+- [ ] Reuse existing experiment code/deployment; adapt dynamic stage context contract, run actual hn01 software checks and resume serial worker.
+- [ ] Publish changes and actual status to SPECTRUM branch.
+
+## Operational findings
+
+Round73 local worker interrupted by host Swap guard; retained PID/group no longer exists, remote GPU idle. Owner reconciled failed local attempt with evidence; temporary maintenance hold prevents duplicate preparation. Guard recovery hysteresis also needs diagnosis: pressure1, reasons=[] may still wait solely for old Swap to fall below4GiB despite steady-run limit6GiB. Preserve protection and report exact decision rather than silently disabling it.
