@@ -113,3 +113,82 @@ method code and formal evidence mode; development data exposure remains visible.
 Preserve formal method/code/design validation, fair S04, freezing, full coverage,
 actual native scorer replay and scientific closure. The handoff replaces old
 Gate0/IPCG prerequisites, not E confirmation evidence.
+
+## Independent stages with pending final scoring (.7)
+
+Use `native_purpose: development_stage` only under adopted C/D. Each scientific,
+developmental native plan has `provenance.native_stage_ref` pointing to a
+`research-native-stage` schema_version1 descriptor. It contains exactly:
+`kind`, `schema_version`, `stage_id`, `stage_kind`, `protocol_ref`,
+`cd_evidence_ref`, `job` (the exact single native job), `scoring_dependency`,
+`dependency_analysis_ref`, `predecessor_receipt_refs`, `required_predecessor_ids`,
+`execution_bindings`, `selection_metric`.
+
+stage_kind is prepare/software_check/calibrate/train/export. Before export,
+arm_role and group are `prerequisite` execution labels, never comparison arms;
+seed records the actual stage seed or0 when inapplicable. Export uses the exact
+real comparison role/group/evaluation seed. Training and evaluation seeds remain
+distinct. `scoring_dependency: deferred` is supported only when the inspected code
+has no quality/reward/filter/early-stop/checkpoint-selection dependency on the
+missing scorer. Cite that actual code analysis. selection_metric is none,
+resource_memory or runtime; quality-driven selection needs its scorer and cannot
+use this deferred route.
+
+`execution_bindings` is exactly `{model_refs,data_refs,selection_refs}`: real pins,
+model/data nonempty, all included in the stage job inputs and identical native
+provenance fields. A later export binds its actual checkpoint, not a future hash.
+The descriptor's exact job/code/outputs are reviewed before dispatch. Stage retries
+are disabled; reconcile the original task before proposing another identity.
+Predecessors are actual archived completed native controller receipts included in
+the current decision's observed receipts. Their stage IDs, program and retained
+outputs must match. No invented future receipt or bare `admitted` flag is valid.
+
+The pinned program has `kind: research-native-stage-program`,
+`stage_contract_version:1`, developmental evidence_mode, normal protocol_id and
+protocol_digest (C.protocol_hash), goal_id, candidate_id, exact cd_development,
+required_groups, seed_policy, full native_eval_contract (or per-group
+native_eval_contracts), and pending_scoring_obligations. Its comparison skeleton
+pins actual sample/label manifests and complete baseline/control implementation
+refs, even when its scorer remains unqualified. All pending obligation IDs must
+exist as pending/blocked in the proposal coverage. Such a program is NOT a valid
+scored protocol; it cannot pass B05/M05, E or scientific closure.
+
+At runtime, use `{NATIVE_STAGE_CONTEXT}` as a command argument. After actual
+controller dispatch and per-attempt authorization, the runner substitutes a new
+immutable context file containing controller task/run/owner/fence, actual native
+run/trial/attempt, stage/program pins, project/workspace roots, dispatch identity
+hash and harness resource context. Do not pre-generate or hash this future file.
+Project wrappers consume this real context; if they require a materialized spec,
+create it in the actual attempt with those identities and retain its provenance.
+Declare output destinations before execution using a unique planned export key;
+record the runtime attempt inside the receipt, rather than needing its future ID
+in the predeclared output path. Stable code deployment is verified separately
+from the runner's copied attempt workspace; do not rewrite historical source pins.
+
+Each stage is proposed after collecting its required predecessor outputs. Native
+Bridge still requires exact remote inputs already synchronized; installing this
+Skill does not deploy project code or create a stage plan automatically.
+
+Later native scoring must use a fully qualified ordinary scientific protocol,
+with native_stage_program_ref pointing to the generation program and
+native_stage_exports entries `{native_stage_ref,execution_bindings}` for each
+actual export. Keep benchmark revision/split, sample/label/selection, metrics,
+format, sampling, budget, contrasts, code/arm requirements and evaluation seeds
+identical. Actual prediction outputs must still join their completed collected
+export run. Changed execution bindings or unscored prerequisite outputs cannot
+close the gate. Full official/faithful scorer validation and real replay remain.
+
+Stage job outputs must be declared beneath `runs/stage-outputs/<native run_id>/`.
+The child writes these relative paths inside its actual attempt workspace; the
+trusted runner exclusively publishes successful outputs to the identical project
+paths. Existing files cause failure, never replacement. Declare these same paths
+in the outer controller task, along with the native run receipt. Stage wrappers
+must not also publish these files to the stable project root. Actual attempt IDs
+remain in execution context/receipts, not in future output filenames.
+
+Each predecessor is authenticated against the controller's registered terminal
+receipt at intake and claim. Cite it in observed receipts and include at least one
+of its real outputs as a current job input; a completed-looking JSON is not a
+predecessor. Required checkpoint/model lineage must also appear in execution
+bindings. M05 validates the linked export program and scored protocol using the
+same correspondence as scored prediction lineage.
